### 2026-10-19
* Anthropic commits 5% of its shares to a wholly owned public benefit fund, subject to stockholder approval [anthropic funding labor] {SL:compute-money}
* Audit of 33,000 agent trajectories finds 76-80% of failed prompt injections were ignored, not refused [prompt-injection agent-security agents evals] {SL:agents-going-wrong}
* Automated repository poisoning of coding agents reports over 60% poisoning success across 384 repositories [agent-security cyber-offense agents open-weights] {SL:agents-going-wrong}
* SenseNova-led evaluation puts GPT-6-Astra at 81.9% on RoboDojo in simulation but 0 of 11 real plug insertions [robotics evals openai agents]
* Reward models fine-tuned to prefer harm in one domain generalised to seven held-out domains [alignment interpretability evals open-weights]
* Claude Opus 5.5 explained half the variance in ML experiment outcomes across 288 proposed ideas [evals anthropic reasoning-models agents]
* Bloomberg review: Russian-linked Matryoshka network aimed 130 fabricated videos at US midterm candidates [influence-ops deepfakes elections threat-intel]
* Zimbabwe police begin texting fines for 4.8 million offences recorded by Harare's AI cameras [surveillance privacy incidents]
* OpenCode co-founder says attackers probed its systems non-stop for 48 hours after the API-key breach [incidents cyber-offense agent-security threat-intel] {SL:china-distillation-export-controls}
* Odisha opposition party files police complaint over AI voice-cloned videos of former bureaucrat [deepfakes elections incidents]
* Army Cyber Command is building ECHOTRIBBLE, AI agents meant to neutralise targets with minimal human oversight [military autonomous-weapons cyber-offense agents us-federal-policy] {SL:ai-weapons-targeting}
* Tech Policy Press names the courts for all eight state suits against OpenAI and four new private cases [openai us-state-policy child-safety incidents] {SL:regulating-frontier-ai-us}
* Nvidia asks Samsung, SK hynix and Micron to build NVHBM base dies on TSMC's 3-nanometer process [nvidia chips compute]
* Some Nscale backers want a $16bn to $19bn IPO valuation against the company's roughly $30bn goal [datacenters funding compute microsoft] {SL:compute-money}
* Samsung Electro-Mechanics wins a 360.5 billion won memory-substrate contract from an undisclosed customer [chips compute datacenters]
* Meta says a Claude tool browsing at four times the normal rate triggered the No Kings Instagram suspension [anthropic incidents agents elections] {SL:agents-going-wrong}
* Reuters: AI industry expected to invest about $1 trillion next year as the Fed treats it as a price shock [compute datacenters us-federal-policy labor] {SL:compute-money}
* Disney agrees to offer jobs to at least 60 Character.AI employees at an estimated $60 million a year [labor child-safety funding incidents]
* World launches World ID for banks, with an AgentKit beta for delegating identity proofs to AI agents [agents agent-security scams-fraud deepfakes]
### 2026-10-20
* MiniMax ships M3.1 Flash, saying agentic tasks cost 70% less than on its previous model [minimax china agents evals]
* Inception releases Mercury 3, a diffusion language model it clocks at 1,068 tokens per second [inception scaling agents evals]
* DeepSeek open-sources DeepInfer, the inference framework behind its production service [deepseek open-weights compute china]
