* FDA digital health director says the agency will draft generative-AI device policy, after more than 300 comments [fda healthcare us-federal-policy]
* OpenAI acquires Orchestra Bio and folds its drug-operations agents into the Rosalind life-sciences suite [openai drug-discovery healthcare agents]
* Study: 97.7% of AI incidents tied to US-listed issuers drew no incident-specific SEC disclosure [incidents us-federal-policy financial-regulation]
* UK publishes a Digital and Technologies Jobs Plan targeting 200,000 entry-level tech jobs over a decade [uk labor education]
* Clearview AI tells UK Court of Appeal the ICO's deletion order would force it out of business entirely [surveillance privacy uk]
* Leaked Anthropic draft prospectus: $16.3 billion first-half revenue, $80.7 billion net loss, nearly $9 billion on compute [anthropic compute earnings datacenters] {SL:compute-money}
* NVIDIA announces supplier capacity expansions, including a $1.1 billion advance for KYEC plants in the US [nvidia chips compute] {SL:compute-money}
* NVIDIA launches containerised DSX POD, saying onsite deployment shrinks from six months to 14 days [nvidia datacenters energy]
* NextDC shares fall 39.5% after Melbourne grid delays force big cuts to its FY27 guidance [datacenters energy earnings]
* Trump urges data centre operators to pay local communities a "dividend" to win support [datacenters us-federal-policy energy]
* SpaceX Q3 revenue $14.6 billion, up 161%, with AI now 52% of income and 1.7GW of compute [earnings compute datacenters spacex] {SL:compute-money}
* Sensor Tower: Meta's Muse reached 10.9 million downloads in 40 days and 2.5 million daily active users [meta agents deployment]
* Eka Robotics raises $150 million at a $1.45 billion valuation for a vision-force-action manipulation model [robotics funding agents]
